KVarN: never flush into a page another KV-cache group has taken (#208, the "!!!!" output).

Backport of kvarn-recycled-pages-0.30.0 to the 0.29.0 pin. The KVarN half is the
vendored backend (kvarn/files/.../kvarn_attn.py) in this same commit; this patch is
the runner-side half, and it is one hunk here rather than two because 0.29 has no
split V2 runner (v1/worker/gpu/model_runner.py does not exist yet).

Why it matters here: KVarN flushes a finished request's last full block to int4 in
the first metadata build after the request leaves the batch, and evicts retired sinks
whenever its pool runs dry. Every KV-cache group on this model shares one tensor per
layer position, so by then the page can belong to another group -- and both runners
write mamba state before they build attention metadata, so a late tile write lands on
state that is already there. The state reads back as NaN and the request prints token
0, "!", from then on. The reported trigger is two requests prefilling in the same
steps while one of them finishes, which is also why PREFIX_CACHE=0 makes it go away.

The guard itself is in the vendored backend: note_scheduled_blocks() records the
pages this step moved to another group, and the next flushing build releases whatever
its pool still holds for them without writing the tile.

--- adapted by hand from cpuchip/qwen38-27b-rtx3090 kvarn-recycled-pages-0.30.0; re-export with scripts/export-patch.sh if it is ever cut from a fork commit ---

--- a/v1/worker/gpu_model_runner.py
+++ b/v1/worker/gpu_model_runner.py
@@ -1230,6 +1230,13 @@
         # stale NaN/data from corrupting attention or SSM computation.
         if scheduler_output.new_block_ids_to_zero:
             self._zero_block_ids(scheduler_output.new_block_ids_to_zero)
+        if self.cache_config.cache_dtype.startswith("kvarn"):
+            # port(kvarn-v2): tell KVarN which pages this step moved to another
+            # KV-cache group, before preprocess_mamba writes state into them
+            # (#208).
+            from vllm.v1.attention.backends.kvarn_attn import note_scheduled_blocks
+
+            note_scheduled_blocks(scheduler_output, self.kv_cache_config)
         if scheduler_output.kv_cache_block_copies:
             copy_kv_cache_blocks_inplace(
                 self.kv_caches,
